                <pb facs="0808" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg674"/>

                <head>No. 488.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Alvensleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 28,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. von Alvensleben</hi>: Responding to your
                    personal note of the 25th instant, I beg to inform you that the question of
                    continued exaction of tonnage dues on the vessels of the North German Line,
                    arriving at New York from Bremen via Southampton, has been brought by me to the
                    attention of the President.</p>
                <p>It is now being investigated, and I trust that all cause of complaint by the
                    German vessel-owners will speedily be removed.</p>
                <p>Yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
